NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.A has 16 observations and 2 variables.

5472       ;
5473       proc hpnlmod data=a out=b;
5474       parms alpha=.45 beta=.05 gamma=-.0025;
5475       x0 = -.5*beta / gamma;
5476       if (x < x0) then
5477       yp = alpha + beta*x + gamma *x*x;
5478       else
5479       yp = alpha + beta*x0 + gamma*x0*x0;
5480       model y ~ residual(yp);
5481       estimate 'join point' -beta/2/gamma;
5482       estimate 'plateau value c' alpha - beta**2/(4*gamma);
5483       predict 'predicted' yp pred=yp;
5484       predict 'response' y pred=y;
5485       predict 'x' x pred=x;
5486       run;


NOTE: The HPNLMOD procedure is executing in single-machine mode.
NOTE: The predicted value of the expression labeled 'predicted' is mapped to yp in the OUT= data set.
NOTE: The predicted value of the expression labeled 'response' is mapped to y in the OUT= data set.
NOTE: The predicted value of the expression labeled 'x' is mapped to x in the OUT= data set.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
